                    "GoldenglowBeaconEnhancementUnit2.Description": "1. Beacon base damage increased (20%>>35%)\nDamage cap increased (110%>>125%)\n\n2. Lightning projectile damage can no longer be dodged and has a small chance to crit (except special monsters)\n\n(Effect activates when placed in inventory)",
                    "GoldenglowBeaconEnhancementUnit3.Description": "1. Beacon base damage increased (20%>>35%)\nDamage cap increased (110%>>125%)\n\n2. Lightning projectile damage can no longer be dodged and has a small chance to crit (except special monsters)\n\n3. +1 Beacon unit\n\n(Effect activates when placed in inventory)",
                    "GoldenglowBeacon.Readme": "Susie's Beacon User Guide",
                    "GoldenglowBeacon.Readme1": "1. Beacon base attack power is 120, attack speed 1.3s.\nInitial attack deals damage equal to 20% of base attack power. Each attack increases this value by 15, up to a maximum of 110% (normally requiring 6 stacks to reach maximum).\n\n2. Beacon attacks have a 10% chance to self-destruct, dealing 375% of base attack damage to enemies within a small area.\n\n3. If a beacon doesn't attack for three seconds, the attack stack effect and self-destruct accumulated probability are cleared.\n\n4. Targeting: After each attack, the beacon re-targets the nearest unit to the player (targeting range is about 15 tiles around the player).\n\n5. Both projectiles and beacon self-destruction track targets. If the target dies prematurely, projectiles will search for new targets within a small range, while beacon self-destruction will target the location where the monster died.\n\n6. \"Beacon Enhancement Units\" take effect simply by being placed in your inventory. Multiple identical enhancement units do not stack effects; only the highest-level unit's effect applies.",


